{{!-- The "write one up" bar at the foot of a GM-prep section.

      TWO classes on the button, doing two different jobs. `stonetop-prep-add-btn` is what it
      LOOKS like: the dashed full-width entry point, stated once in stonetop.css against this one
      class. `{{kind}}-add-btn` is what it DOES: the hook the handler table matches
      (`.<kind>-add-btn`, see gm-prep-tabs.js), which stays per-kind so the four bars keep their
      separate handlers. Splitting them is what stops the styling being a list of kind names
      maintained in a different file from the one that creates them: that list had already
      shipped once without `.site-add-btn` on it, so the Sites tab drew its "Create a site" as a
      bare core button and nothing failed.

      `label` is the whole button text, and `proximity` is threats-only: the Threats tab prints
      one bar per proximity band and the button carries which band it seeds. Absent elsewhere,
      where it renders as an empty attribute the handler simply reads as undefined. --}}
<div class="steading-improvement-add-bar">
	<button type="button" class="stonetop-prep-add-btn {{kind}}-add-btn" data-proximity="{{proximity}}"><i class="fas fa-plus"></i> {{label}}</button>
</div>
